# Rule Content Section

- Write unit tests for every feature.
- Generate enough unit tests to make provable assumptions about the code.
- Generate assertions throughout the code to verify assumptions are always met.
- Do not assume you are able to follow complex logic or class inheritance behavior; instead, believe the results of unit tests.
- For every method, always test expected value ranges.
- Every code project needs a logging facility that is used for all user dialog and debug output.
